Taking a ready thread's process stops it but leaves it on its queue,
so the next turn would run a thread that has no process to run in;
a queue holds only ready threads.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a thread names a queue it is not for

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -476,7 +476,6 @@ void sched_unhost(struct cap *hosted)
         thread_stop(t);
     }
     *hosted = (struct cap){ 0 };
-    thread_settle(t);
 }
 
